---
layout: base.njk
pageType: style-guide
noindex: true
---
{% from "components/style-guide-nav.njk" import styleGuideNav with context %}
{% from "sections/_shell.njk" import enter, pop with context %}
{%- set roles = ["surface", "surface-alt", "surface-raised", "ink", "ink-muted", "ink-inverse", "line", "line-strong", "focus", "success", "success-soft", "success-strong", "warning", "warning-soft", "warning-strong", "danger", "danger-soft", "danger-strong"] -%}
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 md:py-24 lg:px-8">
<p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-brand">Style guide</p>
<h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance">Foundations</h1>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg md:text-xl text-ink-muted">The tokens every page draws from: colour roles, type scale, spacing, radius, shadows and motion. Change the brief, not these pages.</p>
{{ styleGuideNav(styleGuide.pages, page.url) }}

<section class="mt-16">
<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">Colour roles</h2>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-base leading-relaxed">Each role holds a light and a dark value; the page follows the operating system. The two panels force each scheme.</p>
<div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
{%- for scheme in ["scheme-light", "scheme-dark"] %}
<div class="{{ scheme }} rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface p-6 text-ink">
<h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold">{{ "Light" if scheme == "scheme-light" else "Dark" }}</h3>
<ul class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
{%- for role in roles %}
<li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="size-8 shrink-0 rounded-md border border-line bg-{{ role }}"></span><code>{{ role }}</code></li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>
<div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-11 gap-1">
{%- for step in [50, 100, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600, 700, 800, 900, 950] %}
<span class="h-8 rounded-sm bg-brand-{{ step }}" title="brand-{{ step }}"></span>
{%- endfor %}
{%- for step in [50, 100, 200, 300, 400, 500, 600, 700, 800, 900, 950] %}
<span class="h-8 rounded-sm bg-accent-{{ step }}" title="accent-{{ step }}"></span>
{%- endfor %}
</div>
</div>
{%- endfor %}
</div>
</section>

<section class="mt-16">
<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">Type scale</h2>
<div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
<p class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance">Heading one: Industrial automation, simplified</p>
<p class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">Heading two: Built for the people on the floor</p>
<p class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold">Heading three: Commissioning in days</p>
<p class="text-lg font-semibold">Heading four: Safety first</p>
<p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-brand">Eyebrow: Case study</p>
<p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-ink-muted">Lede: Northwind replaces hand-written ladder logic with configuration that plant engineers can read and change themselves.</p>
<p class="max-w-prose text-base leading-relaxed">Body: Lines are capped at sixty-five characters so paragraphs stay readable. Numbers in running text are words below ten and numerals from 10 upward.</p>
<p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">Small: Last reviewed 17 October 2026</p>
<p class="text-4xl font-bold tabular-nums">1,284 <span class="text-base font-normal text-ink-muted">Stat value with tabular numerals</span></p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="mt-16">
<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">Spacing, radius and shadow</h2>
<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-end gap-4">
{%- for step in [1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32] %}
<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 text-xs text-ink-muted"><span class="w-{{ step }} h-{{ step }} rounded-sm bg-brand-300"></span>{{ step }}</div>
{%- endfor %}
</div>
<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-6">
<div class="size-20 rounded-sm bg-surface-alt border border-line"></div>
<div class="size-20 rounded-md bg-surface-alt border border-line"></div>
<div class="size-20 rounded-lg bg-surface-alt border border-line"></div>
<div class="size-20 rounded-xl bg-surface-alt border border-line"></div>
<div class="size-20 rounded-full bg-surface-alt border border-line"></div>
</div>
<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-8">
<div class="size-24 rounded-lg bg-surface-raised shadow-sm"></div>
<div class="size-24 rounded-lg bg-surface-raised shadow-md"></div>
<div class="size-24 rounded-lg bg-surface-raised shadow-lg"></div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="mt-16">
<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">Motion</h2>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-base leading-relaxed">This site runs the <strong>{{ flair.level }}</strong> level of the flair dial (R-TOK-12). Entrances are time-based: an element fades and moves into place over the duration below once it crosses 88 % of the window, columns 90 ms apart, whatever the scroll speed. Depth layers and the progress hairline track the scroll itself. Everything moves only under <code>motion-safe</code>; with reduced motion, without JavaScript and in print the page simply appears.</p>
<div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto">
<table class="w-full min-w-xl text-start text-sm">
<caption class="sr-only">The three levels of the flair dial</caption>
<thead><tr class="border-b border-line-strong"><th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-semibold">Level</th><th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-semibold">Sections</th><th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-semibold">Items</th><th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-semibold">Items below md</th><th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-semibold">Duration</th><th scope="col" class="py-3 text-start font-semibold">Enables</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for l in motionLevels %}
<tr class="border-b border-line{{ ' font-medium text-ink-brand' if l.level == flair.level }}"><th scope="row" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-medium whitespace-nowrap">{{ l.level }}</th><td class="py-3 pe-4 tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap">{{ l.section }} px</td><td class="py-3 pe-4 tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap">{{ l.item }} px</td><td class="py-3 pe-4 tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap">{{ l.itemSm }} px</td><td class="py-3 pe-4 tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap">{{ l.duration }} ms</td><td class="py-3">{{ l.enables | join(", ") if l.enables.length else "rise only" }}</td></tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-muted">The entrance vocabulary of R-MOT-16 and the icon pop, cascading 90 ms apart the way a grid row does; reload with this row below the fold and scroll to it to see it play, or press the button to play it again (the script replays the entrances; without it the row simply stands):</p>
<button type="button" data-replay aria-controls="motion-demo" class="hidden js:inline-flex mt-4 min-h-9 items-center gap-2 rounded-md border border-line-strong px-4 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:bg-surface-alt focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4"><use href="#i-play"></use></svg>Play again</button>
<div id="motion-demo" class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-6 overflow-x-clip sm:grid-cols-5">
{%- set demo = { reveal: true, flair: flair } -%}
<figure><div class="h-24 rounded-lg bg-brand-600{{ enter('start', 0) }}"></div><figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">slide-in</figcaption></figure>
<figure><div class="h-24 rounded-lg bg-brand-500{{ enter('', 90) }}"></div><figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">rise</figcaption></figure>
<figure><div class="h-24 rounded-lg bg-brand-400{{ enter('settle', 180) }}"></div><figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">framed settle</figcaption></figure>
<figure><div class="h-24 rounded-lg bg-brand-300{{ enter('end', 270) }}"></div><figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">slide-from-end</figcaption></figure>
<figure><div class="flex h-24 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-surface-alt"><span class="size-12 rounded-md bg-brand-100{{ pop(demo, 360) }}"></span></div><figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">pop</figcaption></figure>
</div>
</section>
<section class="mt-16">
<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">Sound</h2>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-base leading-relaxed">Sound is off until the visitor turns it on with the <strong>Sound effects</strong> button (in the footer, in the header on wide screens and in the menu on phones); the choice lasts for the tab, and the sounds load only then. Each is synthesised from one scale, so two that overlap agree; the quietest answer the pointer, the loudest confirm what the visitor did. A <strong>Play</strong> button plays its sound once without turning sound on. The rules are bylaw 20 (R-SND).</p>
{%- set sounds = [
  ["hover", "The mouse rests 100 ms on a link, button or card", "A faint high tick; once per target, at most four a second; never on touch or keyboard focus"],
  ["press", "A button is pressed", "A short soft tap, falling"],
  ["pop", "A menu, the language switcher or a tooltip opens", "A small rising pair"],
  ["unpop", "It closes", "The same pair, falling and shorter; silent when another menu replaces it"],
  ["open", "An accordion, FAQ answer or tab opens", "A longer rising pair"],
  ["close", "It closes", "Falling; silent when a sibling in the same group opens"],
  ["sheet", "A dialog, the drawer or the lightbox opens", "A low rising pair, with a breath of air at the expressive level"],
  ["unsheet", "It closes", "The low pair, falling"],
  ["step", "A carousel or the lightbox moves to the next item", "One neutral tick"],
  ["up", "Sound or the dark theme is switched on", "Two notes, rising"],
  ["down", "It is switched off", "Two notes, falling"],
  ["detent", "A slider passes a tenth of its range", "A tiny tick, at most eight a second"],
  ["copy", "A link was copied", "Two bright notes, only once the copy succeeded"],
  ["submit", "A form is sent", "Two notes a fifth apart; an invalid form stays silent"],
  ["in", "A section slides into view", "One soft breath per section, at most one every 1.2 s; none with reduced motion or at the calm level"],
  ["count", "A figure counts up", "Quiet ticks that climb the scale and slow as the figure lands; none at the calm level"],
  ["land", "The figure reaches its value", "One bright note"]
] -%}
<div class="relative mt-8 overflow-x-auto">
<table class="w-full min-w-xl text-start text-sm">
<caption class="sr-only">The sound vocabulary</caption>
<thead><tr class="border-b border-line-strong"><th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-semibold">Sound</th><th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-semibold">Plays when</th><th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-semibold">Character</th><th scope="col" class="py-3 text-start font-semibold"><span class="sr-only">Audition</span></th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for s in sounds %}
<tr class="border-b border-line"><th scope="row" class="py-3 pe-4 text-start font-medium whitespace-nowrap"><code>{{ s[0] }}</code></th><td class="py-3 pe-4">{{ s[1] }}</td><td class="py-3 pe-4 text-ink-muted">{{ s[2] }}</td><td class="py-2"><button type="button" data-sound-demo="{{ s[0] }}" class="hidden js:inline-flex min-h-9 items-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap rounded-md border border-line-strong px-3 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:bg-surface-alt focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4"><use href="#i-play"></use></svg>Play<span class="sr-only"> {{ s[0] }}</span></button></td></tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-sm text-ink-muted">Always silent: a validation error, page navigation, loading, a toast appearing, a video starting, keyboard focus moving, a disabled control, a tab in the background. At most three sounds play at once; an action cuts a hover or entrance sound short.</p>
</section>
</div>
